(3882150, 545907, 74979, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by chaimelle:</b></div><hr/><i> It seems like you took it in bright sunlight, or maybe its just over saturated.  Either way, it has a harsh look to me.  I like the bee on the flower, but it seems too close of a crop on the flower, and a softer light or less processing might bring out more detail in the center of the flower and the bee.  Personally I would try to tone down the yellow overtones in the green of the background, but I am always taking out some yellow so it is probably just me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>looking at this after the fact, &amp; after spending this past week in the Floral side challenge, I agree with just about everything you say here!  Thanks for the feedback..I would have backed off a bit, included the cropped off right edge of the front petal, and probably desat''d the color a bit.  they are very bright like this though, even on rainy days, and one of the reasons they are so welcome in my garden!!</td>', 'Originally posted by chaimelle: It seems like you took it in bright sunlight, or maybe its just over saturated.  Either way, it has a harsh look to me.  I like the bee on the flower, but it seems too close of a crop on the flower, and a softer light or less processing might bring out more detail in the center of the flower and the bee.  Personally I would try to tone down the yellow overtones in the green of the background, but I am always taking out some yellow so it is probably just me.   looking at this after the fact, & after spending this past week in the Floral side challenge, I agree with just about everything you say here!  Thanks for the feedback..I would have backed off a bit, included the cropped off right edge of the front petal, and probably desat''d the color a bit.  they are very bright like this though, even on rainy days, and one of the reasons they are so welcome in my garden!!', '2007-07-08 15:01:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3882182, 546028, 74979, '<td valign="top">Gosh!!  you''re good!! you''ve already got a July entry going??  geez!  I can barely keep up with the flower a day!  Good for you woman!<br/> <br/>on the other hand, it is a good strategy, get your image in there early, &amp; get a spot closer to the front, so people aren''t tired of looking &amp; scoring by the time they get to yours!! <br/>LOL :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-07-08 14:17:30.</i></td>', 'Gosh!!  you''re good!! you''ve already got a July entry going??  geez!  I can barely keep up with the flower a day!  Good for you woman! on the other hand, it is a good strategy, get your image in there early, & get a spot closer to the front, so people aren''t tired of looking & scoring by the time they get to yours!! LOL :)', '2007-07-08 15:16:48.000000', '2007-07-08 15:17:30.000000', 0),
(3882213, 544325, 60862, '<td valign="top">I like the selective desat here.  I agree with the others about the label on the cameraman''s shirt, though.</td>', 'I like the selective desat here.  I agree with the others about the label on the cameraman''s shirt, though.', '2007-07-08 15:31:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(3882215, 546107, 61651, '<td valign="top">This is gorgeous.  I especially love the catch of light on the foreground greenery.</td>', 'This is gorgeous.  I especially love the catch of light on the foreground greenery.', '2007-07-08 15:31:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(3882216, 526509, 61651, '<td valign="top">Nice capture and good framing.</td>', 'Nice capture and good framing.', '2007-07-08 15:33:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(3882218, 545284, 60862, '<td valign="top">Hmm.  I think the DOF here is just a bit too shallow.  Think about what you want to be in focus and use the aperture to get just that in focus.  Here, it seems like it''s the stem that''s the main subject, whereas I''m guessing you wanted it to be the blooms.  But I like the composition and colors very much!</td>', 'Hmm.  I think the DOF here is just a bit too shallow.  Think about what you want to be in focus and use the aperture to get just that in focus.  Here, it seems like it''s the stem that''s the main subject, whereas I''m guessing you wanted it to be the blooms.  But I like the composition and colors very much!', '2007-07-08 15:33:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3882220, 546150, 61651, '<td valign="top">Great framing - I like the chaotic, "going off in all directions" feel.  Good choice not to show the whole ride.</td>', 'Great framing - I like the chaotic, "going off in all directions" feel.  Good choice not to show the whole ride.', '2007-07-08 15:34:49.000000', NULL, 0),
